==Tips & Tricks==
* It is highly recommended to have high mastery on the fruit since unlike all other fruits, it also significantly increases the domain size and the ranges of both Dagger and Fist mode skills of '''[M1]''' , '''[C]''', and '''[V]''' and more space to move around inside the room.
* When first entering a server, Control's move-set is disabled. the player should equip it and wait just around 2 seconds before using a move. This is because, unlike any other fruit, Control loads it's animations every time it enters a server.
* Before using the fruit, the player should be aware of their devices limitations, as Control has extremely high VFX, and often never works properly on low end devices, which may heavily hamper the user's experience. This can also work in reverse, if the user has a high-end device.
* To grind with Control using the M1, it is recommended to click 3 times and wait before clicking again, as the fourth click has high knockback which is not ideal for grinding. Otherwise, '''M1 (Fist Mode)''' seems to be a better candidate for this as it can deal high, continuous damage to NPCs infinitely (if you keep materializing and tossing cubes onto the NPCs), also creating distance in the meantime.
* {{Ability|C}} (Base Mode) can be punished if the opponent spams moves like [[Portal]] {{Ability|Portal|X}} or [[Skull Guitar]] {{Ability|Skull Guitar|X}} fast enough.
* {{Ability|V}} may occasionally make the user stuck, giving a free kill to the opponent.
* Players can jump on the cubes created in fist mode, effectively creating platforms in the air.
* {{Ability|V}} (held) has lower damage than the tap variation.
* Players can charge cubes made by '''M1 (Fist Mode)''' with {{Ability|F}} to deal 50% more damage.
* If the player uses {{Ability|F}} and then activates any other move, the teleport will be '''Ghost''' led. This can trick enemies into thinking the player is about to teleport to that spot, making it a great bait for combos if they fall for it.
* If the user's own device is strong enough, the combination of [[Draco]] V4, paired with [[Primordial Reign]], used with held {{Ability|V}} can completely lag out/disconnect other players in the server.
* Control is especially a good fruit for [[Raids]], as its high-damaging AOE moves, decently far range, high stun potential, and the fact that you can stand over the floating cubes you create from your '''Fist Mode M1'''<nowiki/>'s makes you practically almost untouchable while being able to deal solid damage to enemies from a distance.
* There is a trick to use '''Control X (Mode: Dagger)''' outside domain, by using {{Ability|F}} then use it again then instantly using {{Ability|X}}. However, this is a difficult trick to master.
* During [[Sea Events]] if a [[Terrorshark]] or [[Shark (Enemy)|Sharks]] spawn, the user can lead them to a tall rock on the water. The player will have to stand on the top away from the [[Terrorshark|Terrorshark's]] attack range and then can spam the  '''M1 (Dagger Mode)'''. This can work better with [[Pale Scarf]] and best with [[Leviathan Crown]] accessory. Since these tall rocks are so common and easy to find in seconds, Control is considered to be one of the best fruits for [[Terrorshark|Terrorsharks]].
* During the without room '''[X] Slice N' Dice''' stun, the user can use any '''M1''' to deal more damage during a combo. 

