==Trivia==
{| class="fandom-table"
|'''General'''
* Old Control is used by the Lv. 1250 [[Raid Bosses|Raid Boss]], [[Order]].
* Control and [[Buddha]] are the only fruits that buff weapons.
* '''Dagger Form'''<nowiki>'s</nowiki> {{Ability|TAPMode}}'s Hold/swipe variant cannot be used while using shift lock on pc.
* Control is the second fruit that buffs [[swords]], the first being [[Buddha]].
* The largest item Control's '''[X] (Levitate)''' could lift before its rework was over half of the entire lines of the bridge connecting [[Green Zone]] and the [[Kingdom of Rose]], the resulting explosion is almost as large as the [[Snow Mountain]]s itself, being able to easily devastate the entire area.
* Prior to the rework, Control users could use a glitch with '''[V] Gamma Rush''', where if the move was held for long enough, the user gained the ability to move while holding down the move.
* With a price totaling {{Money|9,000,000}} (formerly {{Money|3,200,000}}), Control is the second most expensive fruit in the game, surpassing [[Kitsune]] and [[Magnet]] and sitting right below [[Dragon]] in value.
* Contrary to popular belief, control can actually be in the normal blox fruits stock.
* Permanent Control shares the same price of {{Robux|4,000}} with Permanent [[Kitsune]].
* Control is the second fruit to have a unique background image in the shop, the first being [[Dragon]].
* The objects that are cut down by the '''Dagger mode''' hold M1s lose their collision physics, but can be stood upon.
* The Control is the second fruit to have an appearance that changes when the physical fruit is held. The first is the physical fruit of [[Barrier]] before [[Updates/20|Update 20]].
* Even after the rework, Control is ineffective for sea events. Moves like '''[X]''' (out of domain) and '''[V]''' cannot hit enemies, so relying on its abilities is not recommended.
* Old Control's [Z] move could be held while casting to make the Area even larger.
* Defeated enemies can still activate their [[Race Awakening]] (V4) even after being bisected. This doesn't stop them from respawning or saving them in any way, though.
* [[Order]] uses the old un-reworked control fruit, while the reworked version is used by [[Zero]].
* For some unknown reason, [[Order]] is able to slice a huge chunk of the Factory on the [[Hot and Cold|Cold]] island, using the old un-reworked Control's '''[X] Levitate'''. This part is very jittery, and has actual physics to it. It also cannot be cut further, and won't detonate if Order despawns. The part can also be flung any and everywhere on the map, reaching a size comparable to [[Bridge]].
** Using [[Dough]]'s Awakened '''[F] Scorching Donut''' on said part completely bugs it out, flinging it far off into the distance.
* The user can only create/cut 8 cubes at a time at any point. They can see this with small glowing cubes hovering over their avatar.
*The [[Kitsune Mask]] visually boosts the meter gain, however it does not actually make it till up any faster.
* Without the final research, Control is the only fruit to have a [[Power Meter]] with no use.
* Control is the second fruit that had a problem with its price ({{Money|3,200,000}}) after its rework. The first being [[Creation]] ({{Money|800,000}}), both maintaining their old value after the rework.
* Despite there being an ‘activated’ icon for the field, it is entirely unused in actual gameplay. This is due to an oversight.

|-
|'''[Z] Domain Control'''
* This move used to last for 35 seconds, then increased to 55 seconds before Update 29. Currently, there is no time limit, however it will disappear after 7 consecutive seconds of leaving the room. Relocating the room using upgrade 2 will not reset the Control meter.
* [[Draco]] V2 flight gains more height while inside of the domain.
* Due to the absurd amount of particles and VFX used in the domain's meshes, it regularly results in major FPS drops and ping spikes, making it an absolute nuisance for medium-lower end devices, even with Fast Mode.
|-
|'''[C] Gamma Blade'''
* The initial VFX on the user's hand can remain stuck if they are laggy.
* Base Form can theoretically do an infinite amount of damage as when it starts pulling back enemies, the user can teleport via a [[Portal]]. This results in a large distance between the enemy stuck in the move and the user, causing the move to keep pulling and damaging the player infinitely. This also cannot be Instinct-tricked.
* Despite Base Form being quite a small blade, it is able to cut extremely huge structures, with the biggest (yet) being the 4 towers around [[Castle on the Sea]].
* Despite Fist Form also being called 'Gamma Blade', it has nothing to do with it whatsoever.
|-
|'''[V] Total Concentration'''
* This is the only move in the game with two cutscenes.
* Before the rework, Control was the first fruit in the game to feature a cutscene.
* This move has the highest mastery requirement for a fruit alongside [[Dragon]] and [[Spirit]], which is 350. Including the upgrade for {{Ability|V}}'s held version makes it 500.
* The tap version of {{Ability|V}} causing a pink/purple domain after missing is confirmed to be a bug by the developers, although a majority of people believe it was a reasonable and intentional design.
* Using the held version will activate the cutscene regardless of whether enemies are present in the domain or not, and it doesn't have to be aimed, as it affects all enemies within the domain. This probably justifies the lower damage than the tap version.
* Due to a glitch, the tap variant may deal lower damage when targeting players, making the move largely pointless as of now.
|-
|'''[F] Transmutation'''
* This move has a longer range than the fully charged [X] move of the [[Cursed Dual Katana|Cursed Dual Katanas]].
* Does more damage when used inside the room than when used outside.
* This is one of the, if not the only move that doesn't halt the passive regeneration of your stamina/health while holding it down.
|}

